@startuml plugin-tool-lifecycle
' ============================================================================
'  agentd - Plugins & Tools: lifecycle, control plane & clients (as-built)
'  ONE question answered end to end:
'    * what a plugin / tool IS and WHERE it lives on disk
'    * how it is CREATED / MODIFIED
'    * how it is DISCOVERED -> becomes a LIVE tool -> reaches an AGENT
'    * which CONFIG LAYER controls what (enable/disable, model, provider, knobs)
'    * how every CLIENT (terminal, desktop UI) sees + edits the same truth
'  Reflects the CODE as it stands today (file refs in the boxes).
'  Render (from this folder):  java -jar ../../../plantuml.jar -charset UTF-8 -tpng plugin-tool-lifecycle.puml
'  (the -charset UTF-8 flag keeps the '·' separators from mojibaking on a CP1252 default)
' ============================================================================

skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam ArrowFontColor #5A5A5A
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #999999
  FontStyle bold
  FontSize 13
}
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #888888
  roundCorner 10
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFF8DC
  BorderColor #C9B458
}

title agentd - Plugins & Tools: lifecycle, control plane & clients (as-built)\nA plugin is a FOLDER; a tool is a class. Discovery -> live catalog -> per-agent view. ONE config.json is the source of truth; every client reads + writes it through the SAME gateway.\ngreen = built today   blue = the Tool contract / catalog   gray = port (interface)   amber = known gap / caveat

' ===========================================================================
' 1) ON DISK -- where plugins & tools LIVE, and how you CREATE / MODIFY them
' ===========================================================================
package "1 · ON DISK  -- where they live / how to author  (no code edits to the core)" #E1F5FE {
  rectangle "**A plugin = a FOLDER**  v2/plugins/<id>/\n----\n**plugin.toml** (manifest, REQUIRED): id · name · kind=native|mcp\n  entry = \"module:register\"  ·  enabled  ·  [requires] os/bins/env  ·  [distribution]\n**entry module**: register(api, ctx) -> calls api.register_tool(MyTool())\n**tool class(es)**: subclass Tool (name·description·parameters·execute\n  + plugin·needs_model·default_model·model_kind)\n**skills/** (optional): advertised like any skill folder\n----\nCREATE a tool  = drop this folder in.   MODIFY behaviour = edit config.json (box 4).\n(built-ins live in the SAME shape under the shipped builtin_plugins_dir)" as FOLDER #C8E6C9

  rectangle "TWO more plugin roots (same manifest, zero core edits):\n · user drop-in dir  = config.plugins_dir  (AGENTD_PLUGINS_DIR)\n · pip packages      = entry_points(group=\"agentd.plugins\")\nMCP plugins: kind=mcp + [mcp] command/url -> an external server (box 6)" as ROOTS #C8E6C9

  rectangle "PORT: PluginApi / PluginContext\nregister_tool(tool) · register_prompt_section(...)\n+ injected runtime handles (browser, task_store, ...)\ninfrastructure/plugins/loader.py" as PLUGINAPI #E2E2E2
}

' ===========================================================================
' THE CONTRACT everything normalizes to
' ===========================================================================
package "THE CONTRACT  ·  application/interfaces/tool.py" #E8EAF6 {
  rectangle "PORT: Tool\nname · description · parameters (JSON schema) · concurrency\nexecute(call_id, params, abort, on_update) -> ToolResult\n---- model-bearing metadata (self-describing) ----\nplugin · needs_model · default_model · model_kind\nresolve_model(config) -> the model this tool will use\n** native tools AND MCP tools normalize to THIS **" as P_TOOL #E2E2E2
}

' ===========================================================================
' 2) DISCOVERY + LOAD  (backend, at daemon boot / on install)
' ===========================================================================
package "2 · DISCOVERY + LOAD  ·  infrastructure/plugins/discovery.py" #EAF6FF {
  rectangle "_discover_manifests(config)\nscan builtin_plugins_dir + plugins_dir for <id>/plugin.toml\n+ pip entry-points  ->  [PluginManifest]  (no plugin code imported yet)" as DISC #C8E6C9
  rectangle "_passes_gates(config, manifest)   -- 4 LOAD gates, in order:\n 1 PROVISIONED (distribution profile)\n 2 ENABLED     (config.plugins[id].enabled -> _gate)   <= main on/off\n 3 COMPATIBLE  ([requires] os/bins/env present)\n 4 ENTITLED    (injected license policy; fails OPEN)" as GATES #C8E6C9
  rectangle "load_plugin_entry(manifest)  -> import module, call register(api,ctx)\n-> Tool objects, tagged with _plugin_id / _plugin_name / _plugin_desc\n(a DISABLED plugin is never imported -> its heavy deps never load)" as LOAD #C8E6C9
}

' ===========================================================================
' 3) COMPOSITION -> the LIVE catalog, then the PER-AGENT view
' ===========================================================================
package "3 · COMPOSITION  ·  main/container.py  +  domain/agent.py" #EDE7F6 {
  rectangle "build the toolset: discovered tools (+ DI-gated browser/computer)\n-> wrap EACH in **GuardedTool** (timeout · retry · loop-detect · marks is_error)" as BUILD #C7B8EA
  rectangle "GLOBAL enablement filter  (domain.select_tools / _filter, by name or glob):\n · tools_disabled  -> drop      · tools_enabled=[] -> allow all\napply_plugin_enablement: drop where plugins[P].tools[T].enabled == false" as ENABLE #C7B8EA
  rectangle "PER-AGENT view  (domain.select_tools):\nagent.toml tools_allow / tools_deny  ->  the tools THIS agent sees.\nOnce loaded a plugin tool is usable by ANY agent -- no special-casing." as AGENTSEL #C7B8EA
}

' ===========================================================================
' 4) CONTROL PLANE -- ONE source of truth + its override layers
' ===========================================================================
package "4 · CONTROL PLANE  -- config is the SINGLE source of truth" #FFF3E0 {
  rectangle "**agentd.config.json**  (loaded ONCE at boot -> in-memory Config; config.py)\n---- who controls what ----\n plugins[id].enabled ............ plugin LOAD on/off        (gate 2)\n tools_disabled / tools_enabled . GLOBAL tool on/off        (name/glob)\n plugins[P].tools[T].enabled .... single tool on/off\n model  ·  cost_efficiency ...... the BRAIN model(s)\n plugins[P].tools[T].model ...... that tool's model\n model_defaults[kind] ........... house default per KIND (vision/image/embed)\n plugins[P].tools[T].provider ... that tool's backend\n plugins[P].tools[T].<knob> ..... behavioural knobs (headless, max_steps, ...)\n reasoning_effort ............... brain thinking level (GLOBAL, not per-tool)" as CFG #FFE0B2

  rectangle "OVERRIDE layers (optional, first hit wins):\n per-call arg  >  **agent.toml** [plugins.P.tools.T]  >  config.json  >  code seed\n · agent.toml = PER-AGENT override (not the plugin's own toml)\n · **.env** = provider API KEYS + AGENTD_* scalar overrides ONLY\n   (models/providers/knobs are CONFIG-ONLY -- never env)" as OVERRIDE #FFE0B2

  rectangle "CODE holds only config-OVERRIDABLE fallback SEEDS:\n tool.default_model · KIND_DEFAULT_MODELS · COMPUTER/EMBED/RESOURCE defaults\n(application/tool_models.py -- every seed beaten by a config line)" as SEEDS #FFE0B2
}

' ===========================================================================
' 5) RESOLVERS -- the ONE place any model/provider/knob is decided
' ===========================================================================
package "5 · RESOLVERS  ·  application/tool_models.py  (config-only)" #E3F2FD {
  rectangle "brain_model(config, agent_model)          -> the reasoning model\nresolve_tool_model(config, plugin, tool)  -> per-call > agent.toml > config > default_model > kind default\nresolve_tool_provider(...)  ·  tool_config(...)  -> providers + behavioural knobs\nSAME functions the runtime AND the settings UI read -> the UI can never drift from what runs" as RESOLVE #BBDEFB
}

' ===========================================================================
' 6) MCP MACHINERY (external servers) -- reused for kind=mcp plugins + data sources
' ===========================================================================
package "6 · MCP MACHINERY  ·  infrastructure/tools/mcp" #E8F8FF {
  rectangle "connect an MCP server -> discover its tools -> wrap each as a Tool\n(server__tool). Data sources page adds these live (mcp.add), no restart.\nSee mcp-architecture.puml." as MCP #C8E6C9
}

' ===========================================================================
' 7) GATEWAY -- the ONE RPC surface every client shares
' ===========================================================================
package "7 · GATEWAY (RPC)  ·  presentation/gateway.py" #FDECEA {
  rectangle "READ (built from the SAME discovery + resolvers, so always truthful):\n plugins.catalog  -> every plugin+tool, on/off, model, provider   (_tool_catalog re-discovers each call)\n models.list      -> brain + every tool model, kind, configKey\n capabilities.list-> tools/plugins/skills/agents in one shape\n config.get       -> values + env presence + model catalogs" as GW_READ #FBD9D4
  rectangle "WRITE:\n config.set { patch }  -> merge into config.json + hot-patch in-memory Config\n config.set { keys }   -> write provider secrets to .env (live)\n restartRecommended=true (most knobs bind at BOOT -> full effect needs restart)" as GW_WRITE #FBD9D4
}

' ===========================================================================
' 8) CLIENTS -- terminal + desktop, both off the same gateway
' ===========================================================================
package "8 · CLIENTS  -- same daemon, same RPCs, same truth" #E1F5FE {
  rectangle "**Desktop UI**  (Settings -> Tools & plugins)\nrenders plugins.catalog: per-plugin card, per-tool on/off + model dropdown.\nModels tab reads models.list/config; saving calls config.set then\nAUTO-RESTARTS the daemon so the change actually applies." as UI #C8E6C9
  rectangle "**Terminal client** (+ any future client)\nreads the same hello / capabilities.list / plugins.catalog.\nPicks up changes on reconnect (the save-triggered restart reconnects all clients)." as TERM #C8E6C9
}

' ===========================================================================
' 9) CONSUMER -- the agent loop
' ===========================================================================
package "9 · AGENT LOOP (consumer)  ·  infrastructure/engine" #EDE7F6 {
  rectangle "per tool call: validate args -> GuardedTool -> Tool.execute(...) -> ToolResult -> LLM.\nThe loop only ever sees Tool.execute -- it cannot tell native from plugin from MCP." as LOOP #C7B8EA
}

' ===========================================================================
' EDGES -- the lifecycle flow
' ===========================================================================
FOLDER --> DISC : plugin.toml discovered
ROOTS --> DISC
FOLDER ..> P_TOOL : tool classes implement
PLUGINAPI ..> LOAD : register_tool(...)

DISC --> GATES
GATES --> LOAD : passes -> import + register
LOAD --> BUILD : Tool objects
MCP --> BUILD : wrapped MCP tools
BUILD --> ENABLE
ENABLE --> AGENTSEL
AGENTSEL --> LOOP : the per-agent catalog
LOOP ..> P_TOOL : executes

' control plane governs each stage (dotted = "controls", labelled with the key)
CFG ..> GATES : plugins[id].enabled
CFG ..> ENABLE : tools_disabled / plugins[P].tools[T].enabled
CFG ..> AGENTSEL : (agent.toml allow/deny)
CFG --> RESOLVE : reads config
OVERRIDE ..> RESOLVE : agent.toml / env / per-call
SEEDS ..> RESOLVE : last-resort defaults
RESOLVE ..> P_TOOL : tool.resolve_model()
RESOLVE ..> LOOP : brain model + tool models

' gateway reads the SAME backend; clients read+write the gateway
DISC ..> GW_READ : re-discovered per request
RESOLVE ..> GW_READ : same resolvers
GW_READ --> UI
GW_READ --> TERM
UI --> GW_WRITE : config.set (+ auto-restart)
TERM --> GW_WRITE
GW_WRITE --> CFG : writes config.json
GW_WRITE --> OVERRIDE : writes .env keys

' ===========================================================================
' NOTES -- the important truths & caveats
' ===========================================================================
note right of FOLDER
  "Drop a folder, it appears":
  a valid plugin.toml is the ONLY
  requirement. plugins.catalog
  RE-DISCOVERS on every call, so a
  new plugin shows in the UI at once.
  CAVEAT: to become CALLABLE live it
  needs a toolset reload -- automatic
  on store-install; a manual drop
  needs a daemon restart (no fs watch).
end note

note bottom of RESOLVE
  ONE resolver, used by BOTH the runtime and
  every client view. Precedence for a model:
   per-call > agent.toml > config.json
            > tool.default_model > kind default
  Models & providers are CONFIG-ONLY (never env);
  only KEYS and AGENTD_* scalars come from .env.
end note

note bottom of ENABLE
  amber CAVEAT: there are TWO tool-disable channels
  -- tools_disabled (what the UI toggle writes) and
  plugins[P].tools[T].enabled. The plugins.catalog
  "enabled" flag reflects tools_disabled only, so a
  tool disabled via the plugins block reads as ON in
  the UI. (Fix: have the catalog honour both.)
end note

note right of CFG
  reasoning_effort is a GLOBAL brain knob
  (config-editable), NOT per-tool. "visibility"
  is not a separate concept -- enable/disable
  IS the visibility axis (a disabled tool still
  shows in Settings so you can re-enable it).
end note

legend bottom
  | Color | Meaning |
  | green | built in v2 today |
  | blue  | the Tool contract / catalog / resolvers |
  | gray  | port = interface |
  | amber | control-plane config / known caveat |
  | dotted arrow | "controls / governs" (config -> stage) |
  | solid arrow  | data / lifecycle flow |
endlegend

@enduml
